External surface (AuroraConfig::externalMetalLayer, off by default)

For embedding the game in a host application (libtww, docs: WW_ONLINE_EMBED.md section 4.2b): Aurora
renders into a CAMetalLayer the host owns instead of an SDL window. SDL starts with its events subsystem
only (no video, which must live on the macOS main thread; no signal handlers, which belong to the host),
the WebGPU surface is made from the layer (SurfaceSourceMetalLayer), the window size comes from
aurora_set_external_size (pushed as AURORA_WINDOW_RESIZED at the next event pump), the window is never
paused, and ImGui runs without its SDL platform backend. aurora_get_external_present_count and
aurora_request_surface_readback (the surface gets CopySrc usage) let the host verify what its layer shows.

